# Copy to .env and fill in. .env is gitignored — never commit it.
#
# THIS FILE IS THE ENGINE'S, NOT A COURSE'S.
#
# A course folder must be the whole course: clone courses/<id>/ onto another
# machine and it has to keep working. So everything a course needs lives in that
# folder's own .env, and nothing here is required for a course to function.
# See courses/GOVERNANCE.md.
#
#   courses/<id>/.env
#     ORALSCALE_SECRET=<64 hex>        the course signing Secret (never shared
#                                      between courses; create it with
#                                      node tools/make-config.js --course …)
#     GENAI_STUDIO_API_KEY=sk-…        only if the course grades with 'genai'
#     GENAI_STUDIO_BASE_URL=…          all three are needed together — with no
#     GENAI_STUDIO_MODEL=…             grader fallbacks, a partial set means
#                                      submissions are NOT graded

# --- Local convenience defaults ---------------------------------------------
# Used only when the course being built does not carry its own. Useful at one
# desk with several courses; never what a deployed course should rely on.
GENAI_STUDIO_BASE_URL=https://genai.rcac.purdue.edu
GENAI_STUDIO_MODEL=gemma4:26b-a4b

# The API key is deliberately absent: it is a credential, so it belongs with the
# course that uses it, not with the engine.

# Silence the "course folder is not backed up" warning, permanently.
# Only set this once you have made a deliberate choice — the warning guards
# against losing a semester of authored questions, and against leaking a bank.
# Courses that ship with the engine never warn.
# ORALSCALE_ACK_COURSE_UNBACKED=1
